                <pb facs="1019" n="905" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg905"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.00 Revolutions/7: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Culbertson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-07-26T14:00:00-05:00">July 26, 1931—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 4:09 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>79. President resigned and is still in Moneda. Already he has requested asylum
                    for his son-in-law and family and I have replied that I cannot admit them to the
                    Embassy unless they are threatened with physical violence and then only
                    temporarily. Civilian junta is forming. Tension has been removed and there is
                    public rejoicing throughout the city.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Culbertson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
